## Project Schedule

(This needs to be reworded - direct from Doug's)

* Week 1: Orientation, literature review, defining scope and objective of assigned projects
* Week 2: Develop project requirements and understand expectations of research output
* Weeks 3-8: Research work – empirical studies, software development, quantitative data analysis
* Weeks 9-10: Finalize projects, prepare presentations and publications, plan next steps in research and professional pathways

## Topic Schedule

*Note that this schedule is subject to change depending on the availability of mentors and speakers*.

* Week 1: The Research Process and Understanding Papers
* Week 2: Responsible Conduct of Research
* Week 3: Performing Literature Reviews
* Week 4: Performing Empirical Research
* Week 5: Statistical Analysis of Datasets
* Week 6: High-Performance Computing
* Week 7: Open-Sourcing your Academic Prototypes
* Week 8: Writing a Research Paper
* Week 9: Presenting your Work
* Week 10: Preparation for Graduate School